# slug: ch06-lower
# source: chapters/ch06.tex:94 (approximate line of \begin{algorithm})
# caption: Lowering Mini expressions to three-address code.
# label: alg:ch06-lower
# require: expression tree node N, instruction list C, counters for temporaries and labels
# ensure: name holding the value of N with its computation appended to C
# keywords: INPUT/OUTPUT/REQUIRE/ENSURE/FOR/FORALL/WHILE/IF/ELSE/RETURN

REQUIRE expression tree node N, instruction list C, counters for temporaries and labels
ENSURE name holding the value of N with its computation appended to C
FUNCTION Lower(N, C)
  IF N is a constant THEN
    make a fresh temporary, emit a materialization, and RETURN it
  ELSE IF N is a variable THEN
    RETURN the resolved binding identifier with C unchanged
  ELSE IF N is an operator node THEN
    lower the left child to a name A
    lower the right child to a name B
    make a fresh temporary T, emit one operation T = A op B, and RETURN T
  END IF
END FUNCTION

